                    "raw": "{\n  \"conversations\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"What is hemoglobin?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Hemoglobin is a protein in red blood cells that carries oxygen throughout your body. In thalassemia, the body doesn't produce enough hemoglobin.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"How often do I need blood transfusions?\",\n      \"answer\": \"For thalassemia major, blood transfusions are typically needed every 2-4 weeks to maintain healthy hemoglobin levels above 9.5 g/dL. Your doctor will determine the exact schedule based on your individual needs.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
